WEBVTT

00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:14,400
I'm feeling well and started to finally put some weight back on naturally.

00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:20,200
I've considered a very short fast to help reset my cells.

00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:23,700
I looked at the prologue therapy fast.

00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:29,200
The prologue fast is a fine day fasting mimicking diet.

00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:36,600
But was wondering if maybe just a simple two-day water juice tea fast might be as effective.

00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:39,100
I've done a two-day fast.

00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:45,600
I've never done a two-day fast, only timed fasting of 13 hours.

00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:48,600
What do you think might be the best thing for me?

00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:53,600
I do not want to lose weight.

00:00:53,600 --> 00:01:02,100
From a tactical standpoint, I never recommend to fast over 24 hours for cancer patients.

00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:10,100
I don't want to increase IGF1 levels and that can have some ill effects on a cancer patient.

00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:13,100
I would not do a two-day fast.

00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:24,100
The prologue therapy five-day fasting mimicking diet is a five-day specific meals that come with that diet.

00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:27,100
It comes all pre-packaged.

00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:36,100
Something you could choose to do or just do 24 hour fast maximum.

00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:39,100
I wouldn't do it any more than that.

00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:48,100
Certainly just sticking to a time restricted eating where maybe you choose to do for two or three days straight.

00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:54,100
Or you only have an eat window, let's say, between 5 and 7 pm.

00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:57,100
And then the next day between 5 and 7 pm.

00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:59,100
And the next day between 5 and 7 pm.

00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:04,100
Therefore you're only doing a 22 hour fast three days in a row.

00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:08,100
That would be better than doing a two-day fast in my opinion.

